# Architecture

Layers (do not mix):

- Tokens / motion: CSS vars `--motion-*` / `--ease-*`. JS timing via `resolveMotionDurationMs`. No raw `duration-[Nms]`, no GSAP/Framer, no `transition-all`.
- `src/components/ui`: generic primitives used in 2+ unrelated surfaces. No hero-kit PNG chrome, no catalog parse, no route I/O.
- `src/features/<domain>/components`: compositions. Feature-local helpers stay next to the feature.
- Adapters (`src/data`, `src/features/<domain>/*.ts`): JSON/schema/lookup/merge. UI never parses catalogs.

Reuse order: existing primitive → new primitive → feature-local split.

Prefer `RivalsCta`, `RivalsTabBar` (chapter nav), `RivalsClipSegment` (compact toggles), `HudReadout`, `HudEmptyState`.

## Anti-god files

- Soft cap ~220 lines, hard cap ~320 for UI files.
- One primary export per file. Subviews and view-models get their own files.
- If a file mixes list + detail + view-model + motion + demo data, split before adding more.
- Extract a primitive at 2+ unrelated uses. Keep kit-only chrome in `features/heroes`.
